    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: QCP scripts whose SBQQ__Code__c exceeds a length threshold or shows signs of heavy nested logic.
Why it matters: Heavy QCPs are the #1 cause of CPQ governor-limit errors. Once script complexity passes a threshold, large quotes start failing intermittently in ways that are hard to reproduce.
Suppress a finding: when the script has been profiled and optimized within budget.
Disable the detector: only when QCP optimization is actively managed. Most should leave this on.</value></values>
